#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186505807 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147415 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "40344731-b251-5ba9-8e05-775144455c95" :knowledge-point/title "Squaring a Fraction"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e28eb08e-4a02-5921-830b-171458c8d0d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{400}{81}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505545}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e28eb08e-4a02-5921-830b-171458c8d0d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{400}{81}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505545} :answer-field/id #uuid "3d270b7c-49c4-5539-9b50-53390b12221d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505639}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b66642ed-0ee4-55e3-841c-23e21fdfce5f" :question/math-academy-id "q-166818" :question/problem "Expressed as an improper fraction, the exact amount of paint available is$\\,${{field-1}}\n$\\,$liters." :question/worked-solution "The exact amount of paint is ${(\\frac{20}{9})}^{2}$ liters.\n\nWriting ${(\\frac{20}{9})}^{2}$ with multiplication signs, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(\\frac{20}{9})}^{2} & ={{\\frac{20}{9}\\times \\frac{20}{9}}_{⏟}}_{2\\text{ times}} \\\\  & =\\frac{20\\times 20}{9\\times 9} \\\\  & =\\frac{400}{81}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{(\\frac{20}{9})}^{2}=\\frac{400}{81}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186505817 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054858 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ef1ed47e-ac17-5e98-8f3c-ea15497f7ff7" :knowledge-point/title "Word Problems"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5c2816d5-5cd7-5758-9767-c5723fe9665f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505290}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5c2816d5-5cd7-5758-9767-c5723fe9665f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505290} :answer-field/id #uuid "a38e32f8-a909-58cc-96de-6fa6c8e64a68" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505681}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c684d185-df16-528a-b856-5845d2d8fecb" :question/math-academy-id "q-166819" :question/problem "The instructions state that $0.6$ liters of thinner should be used for every liter of paint. How much thinner is needed if the painter plans to use $0.4$ liters of paint? Express your answer as a decimal.\n\nThe painter should use$\\,$\n{{field-1}}\n$\\,$liters of thinner with $0.4$ liters of paint." :question/worked-solution "To determine the amount of thinner the painter should use with $0.4$ liters of paint, we have to multiply $0.6$ by $0.4.$\n\nWe proceed by multiplying the two numbers just as we would with whole numbers.\n\nNotice that the second number has a leading $0$, which we ignore during the multiplication:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\begin{aligned} &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\begin{aligned} \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}\\,\\,\\,\\, &  \\\\  &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,0\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,.6\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\ \\,\\,\\,\\,\\times \\,\\,\\,\\, &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,0\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,.4\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,2\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,4\\,\\,\\,\\,\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now count the total number of decimal places in the two factors.\n\nThere is $1$ decimal place in $0.6$ and there is $1$ decimal place in $0.4.$\nTherefore, their product will have $1+1=2$ decimal places.\n\nSo, we take our value of $24$ and add a decimal point to make a number with $2$ decimal places.\n\n$$\n\\,\\overset{↓}{.}\\,\\,\\,{{24}_{⏟}}_{2\\text{ digits}}\n$$\n\nHence, $0.6\\times 0.4=0.24.$\n\nWe conclude that the painter should use $0.24$ liters of thinner in $0.4$ liters of paint."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186505774 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186138368 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "28d5aa07-8c26-5964-bb34-a500d8e0a9e9" :knowledge-point/title "Adding Numbers With One and Two Decimal Places"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bb491334-894c-502e-8a1c-9019aaba8158" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.64" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505467}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bb491334-894c-502e-8a1c-9019aaba8158" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.64" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505467} :answer-field/id #uuid "130e76da-3270-5a38-8e56-8fcce8f0c29b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505615}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5e69e515-4033-521d-8eb1-22e2f3e1c89a" :question/math-academy-id "q-166820" :question/problem "To apply the first coat of paint, the painter mixes $0.4$ liters of paint with $0.24$ liters of thinner. What is the volume of the combined mixture?\n\nExpressed as a decimal, the volume of the mixture equals$\\,$\n{{field-1}}\n$\\,$liters." :question/worked-solution "To determine the volume of the mixture, we need to calculate the sum $0.4+0.24.$\n\nThere is $1$ decimal place in $0.4$ and $2$ decimal places in $0.24.$\n\nTo add the numbers, they both need to have the same number of decimals. Hence, we rewrite the first number so that it has $2$ decimal places:\n\n$$\n0.4=0.40\n$$\n\nNext, we line up the decimal points:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,0\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,.\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,4\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,0\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\ \\,\\,\\,\\,+\\,\\,\\,\\, &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,0\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,.\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,2\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,4\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\  &  &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,.\\,\\,\\,\\, &  & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we proceed by adding the two numbers just as we would with whole numbers:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\begin{aligned} \\\\ \\end{aligned}\\,\\,\\,\\, &  &  \\\\  &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,0\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,.\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,4\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,0\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\ \\,\\,\\,\\,+\\,\\,\\,\\, &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,0\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,.\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,2\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,4\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\  &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,0\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,.\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,6\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,4\\,\\,\\,\\,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume of the mixture equals $0.64$ liters."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186505801 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054862 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f5d09700-00bd-5c67-93cf-f99c574732d7" :knowledge-point/title "Subtracting Decimals: Word Problems"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "09de715f-588e-5d61-86ff-27d04fa29d98" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.46" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505123}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "09de715f-588e-5d61-86ff-27d04fa29d98" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.46" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505123} :answer-field/id #uuid "25c5aa7f-063f-5012-a0d2-bec125ea8a0e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505624}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "aeb902d6-842c-5327-9a4f-f9343ff58a2c" :question/math-academy-id "q-166821" :question/problem "After applying the first coat of paint, the painter had $0.18$ liters of mixture left over. How much mixture did the painter use when applying the first coat of paint? Express your answer as a decimal.\n\nThe painter used$\\,$\n{{field-1}}\n$\\,$liters of the mixture when applying the first coat." :question/worked-solution "In part 3, we found that the painter prepared $0.64$ liters of the mixture.\n\nTo determine the amount of mixture the painter used, we need to calculate $0.64-0.18.$\n\nFirst, we line up the decimal points:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,0\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,.\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,6\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,4\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\ \\,\\,\\,\\,-\\,\\,\\,\\, &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,0\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,.\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,1\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,8\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\  &  &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,.\\,\\,\\,\\, &  & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we proceed by subtracting the two numbers just as we would with whole numbers:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\begin{aligned} \\\\ \\end{aligned}\\,\\,\\,\\, &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\begin{aligned} \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\begin{aligned}14\\end{aligned} \\\\  &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,0\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,.\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,6\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,4\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\ \\,\\,\\,\\,-\\,\\,\\,\\, &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,0\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,.\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,1\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,8\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\  &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,0\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,.\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,4\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,6\\,\\,\\,\\,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the painter used $0.46$ liters of the mixture when applying the first coat."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186505756 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073705 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "cb42b265-bcf6-58ef-aa08-489dec5d1104" :knowledge-point/title "Converting the Result to a Mixed Number"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dbc88f9e-cecb-5783-82a0-96646abc8723" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1\\frac{1}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505528}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dbc88f9e-cecb-5783-82a0-96646abc8723" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1\\frac{1}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505528} :answer-field/id #uuid "83ca6591-abdc-5db7-b63f-855da19951b8" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505667}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "34a9113a-d903-5269-9893-62edd17b6695" :question/math-academy-id "q-166822" :question/problem "In preparation for his entire week's work, the painter purchased $8\\,\\frac{5}{6}$ liters of thinner. Of this amount, he used $7\\,\\frac{2}{3}$ liters. How much thinner did he have left? Express your answer as a mixed fraction.\n\nThe painter had$\\,$\n{{field-1}}\n$\\,$liters of thinner left over." :question/worked-solution "The painter had $(8\\,\\frac{5}{6}-7\\,\\frac{2}{3})$ liters of thinner left over.\n\nWriting $8\\,\\frac{5}{6}$ as an improper fraction, we have\n\n$$\n8\\,\\frac{5}{6}=\\frac{8\\times 6+5}{6}=\\frac{53}{6}.\n$$\n\nWriting $7\\,\\frac{2}{3}$ as an improper fraction, we have\n\n$$\n7\\,\\frac{2}{3}=\\frac{7\\times 3+2}{3}=\\frac{23}{3}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, our problem now is to work out the following:\n\n$$\n\\frac{53}{6}-\\frac{23}{3}\n$$\n\nTo subtract two fractions with unlike denominators, we need to express each fraction as an equivalent fraction with a common denominator.\n\nIn this question, we can make a common denominator of $6.$\n\nTo put $\\frac{23}{3}$ over a denominator of $6,$ we multiply the numerator and denominator by $2:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{23}{3}=\\frac{23\\times 2}{3\\times 2}=\\frac{46}{6}\n$$\n\nWe can now subtract the fractions. We keep the denominator the same, and we subtract the numerators:\n\n$$\n\\frac{53}{6}-\\frac{46}{6}=\\frac{7}{6}\n$$\n\nFinally, we convert back to a mixed number:\n\n$$\n\\frac{7}{6}=1\\,\\text{R}\\,1=1\\,\\frac{1}{6}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the painter had $1\\,\\frac{1}{6}$ liters of thinner left over."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186505729 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073676 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e27e3a75-779a-5817-a2ae-27b58cbac913" :knowledge-point/title "Rounding to the Nearest Whole Number"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "55912364-c928-5e09-9952-20f2493aa37e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "62" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505276}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "55912364-c928-5e09-9952-20f2493aa37e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "62" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505276} :answer-field/id #uuid "3cb9a964-7a5d-5791-a361-fed9b7d0889c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505638}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0001b715-e657-523a-aa88-1e45abcade35" :question/math-academy-id "q-166823" :question/problem "The painter's customer paid the painter $$247.63$ over $4$ days. Estimate the amount of money the customer paid the painter each day by rounding the total amount paid to the nearest dollar.\n\nThe customer paid approximately $\n{{field-1}}$\\,$ per day." :question/worked-solution "To estimate the amount of money the customer paid for each day the painter worked, we need to find an approximation for $247.63÷4.$\n\nSo, we round the dividend to the nearest whole number:\n\n$$\n247.63\\to 248\n$$\n\nNow, we divide $248$ by $4$ as usual:\n\n$$\n248÷4=62\n$$\n\nTherefore, the customer paid approximately $$62$ per day."}]}
